n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a579bce-0249-55ac-9b43-89b6e6ad700d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323243} {:answer/id #uuid "f31aef19-4ebf-54b7-9f2e-e576aecc92d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323244} {:answer/id #uuid "43bc2132-c638-5e1a-8c88-93ab307b1164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323245} {:answer/id #uuid "34bd5f34-00a0-5962-af8c-a323cf1f8a05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323246} {:answer/id #uuid "d96c85d7-b8b6-5a08-8004-e1526b6856bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d96c85d7-b8b6-5a08-8004-e1526b6856bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323247} :answer-field/id #uuid "49bfe50a-e21c-5589-b132-5f674cc79573" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7f951ef-d4f0-53c0-b5fb-64208ef4c99f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73743" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "297f7331-aac8-553f-ba85-90bbc635da4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323250} {:answer/id #uuid "d42041b6-0d0c-57c1-ba96-f611b56a3888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323251} {:answer/id #uuid "5b83f105-9641-50d2-945e-0ab8ddd3b95f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323252} {:answer/id #uuid "d39b1fc1-0fd1-5571-a534-24778b8b105a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323253} {:answer/id #uuid "5a94be43-fac2-5b10-8bc0-57ff3e4cbd7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b83f105-9641-50d2-945e-0ab8ddd3b95f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323252} :answer-field/id #uuid "06d8610c-28df-5a5f-b83b-554ec39b63ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e91f6a97-d964-5da3-939c-23c41ba726cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-73752" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y=10 \\\\ -x+3y=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=5 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=5+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
